- op: discuss  # 11cc
  at: '2026-06-20T19:49:27Z'  # 11cc
  by: agent  # 11cc
  actor: jgstern_agent  # 11cc
  clock: 17  # 11cc
  nonce: 11cc  # 11cc
  message: "SATISFIED across every callable-emitting analyzer (two PRs on origin/dev). PR #4245 (538d5e64e6): homoiconic head-symbol CC walker (_HOMOICONIC_SPECS + _compute_homoiconic_cyclomatic_complexity in core/analyze/cyclomatic.py, dispatched ahead of the node-type walker) wired clojure/commonlisp/scheme/racket/elixir (common) + fennel/janet (extended1) — their control flow is S-expression/call nodes keyed by head-symbol text, not node type, so a BRANCH_NODE_TYPES entry could not see them. Brought the count to 67 languages. PR #4246 (c9f528aa63): the closure re-probe found two residual gaps the per-language sweeps missed — cmake function()/macro() (node-type path: BRANCH_NODE_TYPES cmake={if_command,elseif_command,foreach_command,while_command}) and jupyter notebook Python cells (reuse the py.py Python-AST walkers). CLOSURE RE-PROBE: a static audit enumerated all 86 analyzer modules emitting a function-like Symbol.kind and cross-referenced compute_cyclomatic_complexity wiring; the 8 unwired real analyzers were empirically triaged (run analyzer on a branchy fixture, observe CC) yielding 2 REAL gaps (cmake, jupyter, now fixed) + 6 documented N/A: make (define body flattens to one opaque raw_text node, no control-flow AST), play_routes (single-line route-DSL rows), rust_scip (external SCIP index, no tree-sitter AST), qml + gnuplot (regex line-scanners, no parser), twig macro (body if/for are flat sibling symbols, macro node base-1). The other ~27 static-audit hits are linkers/core-infra that filter or reference kinds, not source-callable emitters. BEHAVIORAL EVIDENCE (live analyzer runs on branchy fixtures, all None pre-fix): cmake my_func CC=5/LOC=15, my_macro CC=3/LOC=8, simple_func CC=1/LOC=3; jupyter classify CC=8/LOC=11, Calc.run CC=3/LOC=7; homoiconic 21 real-grammar per-callable tests (clojure classify=6/process=9, elixir Demo.classify=4, janet process=7, fennel handle=4, etc.) all matched discovery-predicted values; plus the prior 60-language CC suites. check-package-coverage core/common/extended/mainstream all 100% in isolation. The original filed repro (dogfood per-language CC%: non-Python at 0%) is resolved — every callable-emitting language now populates non-null CC/LOC when a control-flow-bearing source AST is available; the 6 no-AST/single-expr constructs are conservative documented N/A. Removed awaits_bakeoff_validation: the closure rests on deterministic per-language unit tests + live repro, not a bakeoff metric."  # 11cc
